{"surah": 110, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِذَا جَآءَ نَصْرُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلْفَتْحُ ", "translation": "When the victory of Allāh has come and the conquest,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَصْرُ", "translit": "ُrْṣَn", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱلْفَتْحُ", "translit": "ُḥْtَfْlٱَw", "root": "فتح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَرَأَيْتَ ٱلنَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِى دِينِ ٱللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا ", "translation": "And you see the people entering into the religion of Allāh in multitudes,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَرَأَيْتَ", "translit": "َtْyَaʾَrَw", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسَ", "translit": "َsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَدْخُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُhkْdَy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "دِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِd", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَفْوَاجًا", "translit": "āًjgāَwْfَaʾ", "root": "فوج"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَٱسْتَغْفِرْهُۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ تَوَّابًۢا ", "translation": "Then exalt [Him] with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him. Indeed, He is ever Accepting of Repentance.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَسَبِّحْ", "translit": "ْḥِّbَsَf", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِحَمْدِ", "translit": "ِdْmَḥِb", "root": "حمد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَغْفِرْهُ", "translit": "ُhْrِfْغَtْsٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَوَّابًۢا", "translit": "āًۢbāَّwَt", "root": "توب"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"3": [{"arabic": "فسبح بحمد ربك واستغفره إنه كان توابا وقال تعالى والمستغفرين بالأسحار وكان صلى الله عليه وسلم يكثر أن يقول سبحانك اللهم وبحمدك اللهم اغفر لي إنك أنت التواب الرحيم (1) وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم من أكثر من الاستغفار جعل الله عز وجل له من كل هم فرجا ومن كل ضيق مخرجا وارزقه من حيث لا يحتسب (2) وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم إني لأستغفر الله تعالى وأتوب إليه في اليوم سبعين مرة (3) هذا مع أنه صلى الله عليه وسلم غفر له ما تقدم من ذنبه وما تأخر وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم إنه ليغان على قلبي حتى إني لأستغف", "english": "God Most High said: {«والذين إذا فعلوا فاحشة أو ظلموا أنفسهم ذكروا الله فاستغفروا لذنوبهم»} — \"And those who, when they commit an indecency or wrong themselves, remember God and seek forgiveness for their sins\" {آل عمران/135}.", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 246", "section_title_en": "On Seeking Forgiveness (Al-Istighfar) — Section 246", "section_index": 246, "anchors": "- Root: ذنب (dhanb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of \"tail\" or \"taking hold of a tail\"; extended to signify a sin as that which trails behind and follows a person.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الذنب في الأصل: الأخذ بذنب الشيء\" — sin is that by which one is seized and held accountable; used metaphorically for a fault that clings to its perpetrator.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: tail of an animal. Metaphorical: \"هو من الأذناب\" — one who follows; sin as that which trails the soul and must be severed through repentance.\n- Root: غفر (ghafara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Covering, veiling, protecting from defilement; a shield or helmet (المغفر).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الغفران والمغفرة من الله هو أن يصون العبد من أن يمسه العذاب\" — divine forgiveness is God's protection of the servant from being touched by punishment.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to cover and protect. Metaphorical: God's \"covering\" of sins — not merely erasure, but active safeguarding of the sinner from consequence.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The frequent interposition of \"يا رب\" and vocative constructions between the subject and predicate in supplicatory sentences, as in \"اللهم اغفر لي,\" where the vocative particle governs the imperative verb's addressee, reflecting the grammatical permissibility of separation between governing and governed elements in invocational speech.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 1203], [2, 1203, 2507], [3, 2507, 3229], [4, 3229, 4093], [5, 4093, 5383]], "2": [[1, 350, 1491], [2, 1491, 2678], [3, 2678, 4031], [4, 4031, 4491], [5, 4491, 5135], [6, 5135, 5862], [7, 5862, 7316]], "3": [[1, 400, 1546], [2, 1546, 2495], [3, 2495, 3363], [4, 3363, 5192], [5, 5192, 6246], [6, 6246, 7080], [7, 7080, 8892]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 400, 1826], [2, 1826, 4005], [3, 4005, 5211], [4, 5211, 6655], [5, 6655, 8811]], "2": [[1, 400, 2373], [2, 2373, 4425], [3, 4425, 6763], [4, 6763, 7558], [5, 7558, 8672], [6, 8672, 9929], [7, 9929, 12442]], "3": [[1, 400, 2455], [2, 2455, 4157], [3, 4157, 5714], [4, 5714, 8994], [5, 8994, 10883], [6, 10883, 12378], [7, 12378, 15629]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 240, 1297], [2, 1297, 3390], [3, 3390, 4077], [4, 4077, 4923], [5, 4923, 6370]], "2": [[1, 390, 1749], [2, 1749, 3137], [3, 3137, 4883], [4, 4883, 5374], [5, 5374, 6205], [6, 6205, 6960], [7, 6960, 9410]], "3": [[1, 20, 1254], [2, 1254, 2276], [3, 2276, 3211], [4, 3211, 5430], [5, 5430, 6502], [6, 6502, 7674], [7, 7674, 11060]]}, "abdulbasit_warsh": {"110:1": [[1, 400, 1080], [2, 1160, 1725], [3, 1805, 2370], [4, 2450, 3130], [5, 3210, 4120]], "110:2": [[1, 400, 1310], [2, 1390, 2185], [3, 2265, 3175], [4, 3255, 3705], [5, 3785, 4350], [6, 4430, 5110], [7, 5190, 6215]], "110:3": [[1, 400, 1080], [2, 1160, 1840], [3, 1920, 2485], [4, 2565, 3705], [5, 3785, 4580